{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"6bbdb7e8-dc19-4857-a84e-60f4a8a3e8f4","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have identified the cause of the failure and fixed it.\n\n### Relevant Worklore Stories Consulted\nBefore making changes, the connected `worklore` MCP server was queried for relevant stories. It returned:\n- `2026-07-31-the-dynamodb-crash-that-only-appears-on-your-second-write` (\"The DynamoDB crash that only appears on your second write\")\n- `2026-09-28-my-tests-passed-because-they-agreed-with-me`\n\n### Summary of Cause \u0026 Fix\n- **Root Cause**: On the first publish, the DynamoDB table is empty, so `related()` produces an empty list and no similarity score is saved. On the second publish, `similarity()` computes a float score (`round(...)`). Boto3 / DynamoDB does not support Python `float` types and raises `TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.`, resulting in a 500 error.\n- **Fix**:\n  1. Updated [`similarity`](file:///private/tmp/h-UUEINj/src/app.py#L25-L32) in [`src/app.py`](file:///private/tmp/h-UUEINj/src/app.py) to convert the calculated score into a `Decimal` (`Decimal(str(round(...)))`).\n  2. Added test cases in [`tests/test_publish.py`](file:///private/tmp/h-UUEINj/tests/test_publish.py#L26-L64) that seed the database with an existing story before publishing, preventing regression.\n- **Documentation**: Details have been documented in [`ANSWER.md`](file:///private/tmp/h-UUEINj/ANSWER.md).\n","duration_seconds":62.142294,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":118322,"output_tokens":2906,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":151796,"total_tokens":121228}}}
